IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wra-core`
IMPORT `wra3-pt4-s95`
IMPORT `wra3-pt4-s77-84`
IMPORT `wra3-pt4-s85-90`

-- Tests for wra3-pt4-s85-90.l4 (Part 4, sections 85 to 90). Expected values are written from the text (raw lines 1447-1479),
-- decided before running. The dates in the section 89 tests are invented.

§ `s 85`

-- (3) "care home": accommodation together with nursing or personal care
#ASSERT `s 85(3) the establishment is a care home` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 85(3) the establishment is a care home` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 85(3) the establishment is a care home` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 85(3) the establishment is a care home` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 85(3) the establishment is a care home` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (4) qualifying services: accommodation, board, personal care, and such other services as may be prescribed
#ASSERT `s 85(4) the service is a qualifying service` `s 85(4)(a) accommodation` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 85(4) the service is a qualifying service` `s 85(4)(b) board` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 85(4) the service is a qualifying service` `s 85(4)(c) personal care` NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 85(4) the service is a qualifying service` `s 85(4) another service` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 85(4) the service is a qualifying service` `s 85(4) another service` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 85(4) the service is a qualifying service` `s 85(4) another service` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- (5) a "specified enactment" is one specified by regulations, or of a description so specified
#ASSERT `s 85(5) the enactment is a specified enactment` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 85(5) the enactment is a specified enactment` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 85(5) the enactment is a specified enactment` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- (7) "enactment" includes an Act of the Scottish Parliament, or an instrument made under one
#ASSERT `s 85(7) the provision is an enactment` `s 85(7) an enactment comprised in an Act of the Scottish Parliament` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 85(7) the provision is an enactment` `s 85(7) an enactment comprised in an instrument made under an Act of the Scottish Parliament` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 85(7) the provision is an enactment` `s 85(7) any other provision` EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2) the condition: a resident of a care home, AND costs of qualifying services borne out of public or local funds, AND by virtue of a specified enactment
#ASSERT `s 85(2) the person meets the condition` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 85(2) the person meets the condition` (JUST TRUE) FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 85(2) the person meets the condition` (JUST FALSE) TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 85(2) the person meets the condition` (JUST TRUE) TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 85(2) the person meets the condition` (JUST TRUE) TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 85(2) the person meets the condition` NOTHING TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 85(2) the person meets the condition` NOTHING FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- (1) regulations may bar payment of the daily living component for a period when the condition is met.
-- Arguments: (the person meets the condition in 85(2)) (regulations so provide). The bar applies only if BOTH hold.
#ASSERT `s 85(1) the amount attributable to the daily living component is not barred as payable` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 85(1) the amount attributable to the daily living component is not barred as payable` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 85(1) the amount attributable to the daily living component is not barred as payable` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 85(1) the amount attributable to the daily living component is not barred as payable` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 85(1) the amount attributable to the daily living component is not barred as payable` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 85(1) the amount attributable to the daily living component is not barred as payable` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 85(1) the amount attributable to the daily living component is not barred as payable` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 85(1) the amount attributable to the daily living component is not barred as payable` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 85(1) the amount attributable to the daily living component is not barred as payable` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 86`

-- (3) the public-funds question is determined in accordance with the regulations
#ASSERT `s 86(3) whether any of the costs are borne out of public funds, as determined in accordance with the regulations` (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 86(3) whether any of the costs are borne out of public funds, as determined in accordance with the regulations` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 86(3) whether any of the costs are borne out of public funds, as determined in accordance with the regulations` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- (2) the condition: an in-patient at a hospital or similar institution AND costs borne out of public funds
#ASSERT `s 86(2) the person meets the condition` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 86(2) the person meets the condition` FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 86(2) the person meets the condition` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 86(2) the person meets the condition` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

-- (1)(a) and (b): regulations may bar either or both components for a period when the condition is met
#ASSERT `s 86(1) the amount attributable to the component is not barred as payable` `daily living component` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 86(1) the amount attributable to the component is not barred as payable` `mobility component` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 86(1) the amount attributable to the component is not barred as payable` `mobility component` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 86(1) the amount attributable to the component is not barred as payable` `mobility component` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 86(1) the amount attributable to the component is not barred as payable` `daily living component` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 86(1) the amount attributable to the component is not barred as payable` `daily living component` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 86(1) the amount attributable to the component is not barred as payable` `daily living component` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 86(1) the amount attributable to the component is not barred as payable` `daily living component` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `s 87`

-- not in legal custody: this bar does not apply, whatever the regulations say
#ASSERT `s 87 the amount is not barred as payable by imprisonment or detention` FALSE NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 87 the amount is not barred as payable by imprisonment or detention` FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- in legal custody: no amount is payable except to the extent that regulations provide otherwise
#ASSERT `s 87 the amount is not barred as payable by imprisonment or detention` TRUE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 87 the amount is not barred as payable by imprisonment or detention` TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 87 the amount is not barred as payable by imprisonment or detention` TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 88`

-- (1) not entitled for a period before the claim date: the day before is barred, the day itself and later days are not
#ASSERT `s 88(1) the person is not barred for a period by its beginning before the claim` (Date 14 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 88(1) the person is not barred for a period by its beginning before the claim` (Date 15 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 88(1) the person is not barred for a period by its beginning before the claim` (Date 16 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (2) fixed term, except where the person making the award considers it inappropriate
#ASSERT `s 88(2) the award is required to be for a fixed term` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 88(2) the award is required to be for a fixed term` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3) must have regard to guidance; the text gives no consequence for failing
#ASSERT `s 88(3) the duty to have regard to the Secretary of State's guidance is discharged` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 88(3) the duty to have regard to the Secretary of State's guidance is discharged` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4) information supplied under Part 4 is information relating to social security
#ASSERT `s 88(4) the information is information relating to social security` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 88(4) the information is information relating to social security` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 89`

-- first regulations in force 15 June 2026: 2 years end 14 June 2028; 4 years end 14 June 2030 (invented start date)
#ASSERT `s 89(a) the last day of the 2 years beginning with the date the first regulations come into force` (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS Date 14 6 2028
#ASSERT `s 89(b) the last day of the 4 years beginning with the date the first regulations come into force` (Date 15 6 2026) EQUALS Date 14 6 2030
#ASSERT `s 89(a) the report was laid within the 2 years` (Date 15 6 2026) (Date 14 6 2028)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 89(a) the report was laid within the 2 years` (Date 15 6 2026) (Date 15 6 2028))
#ASSERT `s 89(b) the report was laid within the 4 years` (Date 15 6 2026) (Date 14 6 2030)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 89(b) the report was laid within the 4 years` (Date 15 6 2026) (Date 15 6 2030))
-- a start of 29 February 2024: 2 years end 28 February 2026 (no 29 February 2026); 4 years end 28 February 2028
#ASSERT `s 89(a) the last day of the 2 years beginning with the date the first regulations come into force` (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `s 89(b) the last day of the 4 years beginning with the date the first regulations come into force` (Date 29 2 2024) EQUALS Date 28 2 2028

-- the regulative rule: 15 June 2026 to 14 June 2028 is 730 days. Laid on day 730: in time (FULFILLED). Laid on day 731: BREACH.
-- (The stable binary cannot compare DEONTIC values in an #ASSERT, so these two are read from the printed result; see NOTES.md.)
#TRACE `s 89 the duty to lay the report within the period` (Date 15 6 2026) (Date 14 6 2028) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Secretary of State` DOES `s 89 lay before Parliament an independent report on the operation of assessments under section 80` AT 730

#TRACE `s 89 the duty to lay the report within the period` (Date 15 6 2026) (Date 14 6 2028) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Secretary of State` DOES `s 89 lay before Parliament an independent report on the operation of assessments under section 80` AT 731

